{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>First time</b><br>עיניך יונים. (כיונים) like אש אוכלה [it is]:" "<b>Second time</b><br>He answered: You are beautiful; your eyes are doves. Like a dove, which loves its mate and does not leave it:" "<b>Third time</b><br>The Shekhinah answered: Now I will adorn you with poems; prophets I shall send to you, and they are your eyes:"], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites the phrase אש אוכלה (Deut. 4:24 etc.) as a grammatical parallel for a noun functioning adjectivally; the bracketed 'הוא' appears to be his laconic gloss that the construction 'is' of that type."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:54.192200662Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}